<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Andecavi</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gallic people of Anjou whose leader Dumnacus fought one of the last campaigns against Rome in 51 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Andecavi, called Andes by Caesar, lived on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angers">Angers</a>. Caesar quartered legions among them in 57 BCE and records that they joined the revolt of 52 BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of their institutions beyond their war leaders.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 51 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dumnacus">Dumnacus</a> besieged the pro-Roman <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/pictones">Pictones</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Lemonum</a>, but was defeated by Caesar's legate Gaius Fabius and fled. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> their chief town was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angers">Juliomagus</a>, later called Andecavi, the origin of Angers and of the name <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-anjou">Anjou</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/andecavi.jpg" alt="Andecavi" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: cgb · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stat%C3%A8re_d%E2%80%99%C3%A9lectrum_%E2%80%9Caux_aigrettes%E2%80%9D_frapp%C3%A9_par_les_And%C3%A9caves_(r%C3%A9gion_d%27Angers).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Dumnacus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Andes</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=andecavi" aria-label="Andecavi on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4746 544 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Andecavi lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5066 800h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5066 800h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day France. <a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=andecavi">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

